   {
    "id": 145,
    "type": "mask_accordions",
    "colPos": 0,
    "categories": "",
    "appearance": {
     "layout": "default",
     "frameClass": "default",
     "spaceBefore": "",
     "spaceAfter": ""
    },
    "content": {
     "header": "Three families",
     "subheader": "",
     "headerLayout": 0,
     "headerPosition": "",
     "headerLink": "",
     "type": "mask_accordions",
     "title": "The owners",
     "text": "",
     "accordion": [
      {
       "uid": "5",
       "title": "The Posch family - the visionaries",
       "info": "",
       "text": "<p>‘We had a vision: of a journey to rediscover ourselves, to acknowledge and take a step towards the positive feeling that arises out of a sense of freedom and vitality. With the courage and the willingness to challenge the boundaries of our comfort zones, we wanted to create a place where origins, simplicity and the archaic take centre stage and utterly captivate. A space for unique experiences and new, inspiring adventures that fill our guests with pride and happiness that they can take home.’ Dominik and Amelie Posch</p>",
       "linktext": "",
       "link": ""
      },
      {
       "uid": "6",
       "title": "The Spielmann family - the strategists",
       "info": "",
       "text": "<p>‘As strategic, financial and process consultants, we provided our expertise to overcome the hurdles of realising this special and remote project in the midst of nature. This unique setting on the Ehrwalder Alm Alpine pasture is both a challenge and an opportunity to, with the company of great partners, redefine Alpine tourism and offer a way of living that bring people back their origins and roots.’&nbsp; Martin and Christina Spielmann</p>",
       "linktext": "",
       "link": ""
      },
      {
       "uid": "7",
       "title": "Andreas Mader - the constructor",
       "info": "",
       "text": "<p>‘As a timber construction and carpentry specialist, this was a unique opportunity to create a showcase project for sustainable tourism at a former company site, surrounded by nature, and to realise it together with partners that can contribute hotel industry expertise. We created a destination out of original, local materials that offers a glimpse into real, original forest living in the Alps. A place where you want to stay.’ Andreas Mader</p>",
       "linktext": "",
       "link": ""
      }
     ]
    }
   },
